anguage\":\"zh-Hant-HK\",\"regularMarketTime\":{\"raw\":1792785600,\"fmt\":\"4:00PM EDT\"},\"quoteType\":\"EQUITY\",\"typeDisp\":\"股票\",\"lastClosePriceToNNWCPerShare\":{\"raw\":152.99624640669663,\"fmt\":\"153.00\"},\"tradeable\":false,\"exchangeTimezoneName\":\"America/New_York\",\"cryptoTradeable\":false,\"exchangeDataDelayedBy\":15,\"firstTradeDateMilliseconds\":917015400000,\"exchangeTimezoneShortName\":\"EDT\",\"fulldayPrice\":{\"raw\":210.96,\"fmt\":\"210.96\"},\"hasPrePostMarketData\":true,\"regularMarketPrice\":{\"raw\":210.96,\"fmt\":\"210.96\"},\"customPriceAlertConfidence\":\"NONE\",\"marketState\":\"CLOSED\",\"market\":\"us_market\",\"quoteSourceName\":\"Delayed Quote\",\"lastCloseTevEbitLtm\":{\"raw\":25.815627,\"fmt\":\"25.82\"},\"priceHint\":2,\"sourceInterval\":15,\"exchange\":\"NMS\",\"region\":\"HK\",\"triggerable\":false}],\"useRecords\":false,\"predefinedScr\":true,\"versionId\":10,\"creationDate\":1473802561519,\"lastUpdated\":1747133602605,\"isPremium\":false,\"iconUrl\":\"https://s.yimg.com/cv/apiv2/fin/img/assets/predefined_screeners/analytics.png\"}],\"error\":null}}"}</script>
			<script type="application/json" data-sveltekit-fetched data-url="https://query1.finance.yahoo.com/ws/screeners/v1/finance/calendar-events?countPerDay=25&amp;economicEventsHighImportanceOnly=true&amp;economicEventsRegionFilter=&amp;endDate=1792782000000&amp;modules=economicEvents&amp;startDate=1792695600000&amp;lang=zh-Hant-HK&amp;region=HK" data-hash="186cp8h" data-ttl="60">{"status":200,"statusText":"","headers":{"cache-control":"public, max-age=60, stale-while-revalidate=120"},"body":"{\"finance\":{\"result\":{\"economicEvents\":[{\"timestamp\":1792641600000,\"timestampString\":\"2026-10-22\",\"timezone\":\"America/New_York\",\"count\":7,\"totalCount\":7,\"records\":[{\"economicEvents\":true,\"event\":\"CPI, Overall Nationwide\",\"countryCode\":\"JP\",\"eventTime\":1792711800000,\"period\":\"Sep\",\"actual\":\"2.1\",\"prior\":\"1.9\",\"description\":\"The consumer price index (CPI) is a measure of change over a specified period of time in the general level of prices of goods and services that a given population acquires, uses or pays for consumption. It compares a household's cost for a specific basket of finished goods and services with the cost of the same basket during an earlier benchmark period \"},{\"economicEvents\":true,\"event\":\"CPI, Core Nationwide YY\",\"countryCode\":\"JP\",\"eventTime\":1792711800000,\"period\":\"Sep\",\"actual\":\"2.1\",\"prior\":\"1.7\",\"description\":\"The consumer price index (CPI) is a measure of change over a specified period of time in the general level of prices of goods and services that a given population acquires, uses or pays for consumption. It compares a household's cost for a specific basket of finished goods and services with the cost of the same basket during an earlier benchmark period. \"},{\"economicEvents\":true,\"event\":\"GfK/NIM Consumer Confidence\",\"countryCode\":\"GB\",\"eventTime\":1792710060000,\"period\":\"Oct\",\"actual\":\"-24\",\"prior\":\"-13\",\"description\":\"The UK Consumer Confidence Survey from GfK NOP was conducted amongst a sample of 2000 individuals aged 16+ on behalf of the European Commission.Quotas are imposed on age, sex, region and social class to ensure the final sample is representative of the UK population. The figures contained within the Consumer Confidence Barometer have an estimated margin of error of +/-2%.Results for the Consumer Confidence Barometer are available on the last working day of each month at 10.30am \"},{\"economicEvents\":true,\"event\":\"Consumer Confid. Flash *\",\"countryCode\":\"EU\",\"eventTime\":1792677600000,\"period\":\"Oct\",\"actual\":\"-17.9\",\"prior\":\"-16.5\",\"revisedFrom\":\"-16.8\",\"description\":\" The indicator is the arithmetic average of the balances (%) for the present and the future business situation, and for stocks - with inverted sign. Balances: i.e. differences between the percentages of respondents giving positive and negative replies. \"},{\"economicEvents\":true,\"event\":\"Producer Prices YY\",\"countryCode\":\"CA\",\"eventTime\":1792672200000,\"period\":\"Sep\",\"actual\":\"14.5\",\"prior\":\"13.5\",\"revisedFrom\":\"13.2\",\"description\":\"The Industrial Product Price index (IPPI) reflects the prices that producers receive as the goods leave the plant gate. It does not reflect what the consumer pays. Unlike the consumer price index, the IPPI excludes indirect taxes and all the costs that occur between the time when a goods leaves the plant and the time when the final user takes possession of it, including the transportation, wholesale and retail costs. \"},{\"economicEvents\":true,\"event\":\"Producer Prices MM\",\"countryCode\":\"CA\",\"eventTime\":1792672200000,\"period\":\"Sep\",\"actual\":\"2\",\"prior\":\"1.3\",\"revisedFrom\":\"1.2\",\"description\":\"The Industrial Product Price index (IPPI) reflects the prices that producers receive as the goods leave the plant gate. It does not reflect what the consumer pays. Unlike the consumer price index, the IPPI excludes indirect taxes and all the costs that occur between the time when a goods leaves the plant and the time when the final user takes possession of it, including the transportation, wholesale and retail costs. \"},{\"economicEvents\":true,\"event\":\"New Housing Price Index*\",\"countryCode\":\"CA\",\"eventTime\":1792672200000,\"period\":\"Sep\",\"actual\":\"-0.2\",\"prior\":\"-0.1\",\"description\":\"The index measures changes of contractor's selling prices of new residential houses. House price index is a statistic designed to reflect the average change of house prices across the country or a certain area. It ensures that the relative importance of different property types in different regions remains fixed throughout the life of the index. Different adjustment must be used as no two houses are identical. Therefore characteristics such as physical attributes of a house or its location should be included in the calculation if the index. \"}]},{\"timestamp\":1792728000000,\"timestampString\":\"2026-10-23\",\"timezone\":\"America/New_York\",\"count\":4,\"totalCount\":4,\"records\":[{\"economicEvents\":true,\"event\":\"U Mich Sentiment Final*\",\"countryCode\":\"US\",\"eventTime\":1792764000000,\"period\":\"Oct\",\"actual\":\"48\",\"prior\":\"46.3\"},{\"economicEvents\":true,\"event\":\"Retail Sales Ex-Autos MM\",\"countryCode\":\"CA\",\"eventTime\":1792758600000,\"period\":\"Aug\",\"actual\":\"1.2\",\"prior\":\"-0.7\",\"revisedFrom\":\"-0.8\",\"description\":\"The North American Industry Classification System (NAICS) was introduced in June 2004. \"},{\"economicEvents\":true,\"event\":\"Retail Sales YY\",\"countryCode\":\"GB\",\"eventTime\":1792735200000,\"period\":\"Sep\",\"actual\":\"0.8\",\"prior\":\"2.4\",\"revisedFrom\":\"2.7\",\"description\":\"Retail sales data represents total consumer purchase from retail stores. It provides valuable information about consumer spending which makes up the consumption part of GDP. The most volatile components like autos, gas prices and food prices are often removed from the report to show more underlying demand patterns as changes in sales in these categories are frequently a result of price changes. It is not adjusted for inflation. Spending on services is not included. Rising retail sales indicate stronger economic growth. However, if the increase is larger than forecast, it may be inflationary. \"},{\"economicEvents\":true,\"event\":\"Retail Sales MM\",\"countryCode\":\"GB\",\"eventTime\":1792735200000,\"period\":\"Sep\",\"actual\":\"-0.4\",\"prior\":\"0.5\",\"revisedFrom\":\"0.7\",\"description\":\"Retail sales data represents total consumer purchase from retail stores. It provides valuable information about consumer spending which makes up the consumption part of GDP. The most volatile components like autos, gas prices and food prices are often removed from the report to show more underlying demand patterns as changes in sales in these categories are frequently a result of price changes. It is not adjusted for inflation. Spending on services is not included. Rising retail sales indicate stronger economic growth. However, if the increase is larger than forecast, it may be inflationary. \"}]}]},\"error\":null}}"}</script>
